      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Predicting downturns based on specific ethnic or cultural shifts is often a flawed approach, but in real estate, the most predictive factor is usually a rapid influx of lower-income populations without corresponding economic investment. When the local tax base weakens due to a sudden shift away from established, higher-earning residents, commercial viability suffers quickly. You should flag areas where the median household income drops significantly while the population density increases rapidly, regardless of the specific cultural makeup.",
